{%- comment -%}
  Product pictures and option names as data, for the scripts that paint
  products without Liquid: the cart drawer (lines painted from /cart.js),
  its pair offer, and the cart page's pair chooser. One small JSON per page,
  read by assets/zorev.js (window.ZorevCart.media(variantId)):

    { "studio": true|false,
      "v": { "<variant id>": { "p": <product id>, "src": "<url>|null",
                               "label": "Black" } } }

  src   snippets/studio-image's choice for the option, as a URL at 240w (a
        72 px thumbnail at 3x, never upscaled): the maker's studio packshot
        when Theme settings > Studio images is on and a slot names this
        variant (for HOYGI its clean cutout slot, see below), else the
        variant's own photograph, else the product's featured image. null
        when there is no picture: the drawer then uses the line's own image.
  label snippets/zvlabel's name for the option ("Citrus (men's)"), empty for
        a product with a single variant, so the drawer, the cart page and the
        product page all name an option the same way.

  Bounded to the first 24 products: this catalogue has two, and the loop
  must never become the slow part of a page.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign studio_on = false
  if settings.studio_mode == 'on'
    assign studio_on = true
  endif
  comment
    Thumbnail slot. HOYGI (Theme settings > Offers > pair product B) has
    the maker's balm photo in its first studio slot (a busy still life of
    leaves and stone, unreadable at 72 px) and the clean stick-and-box
    cutout in its second, so thumbnails use the second slot whenever that
    variant has one. Every other option keeps its first slot (GODA: one
    packshot per option). cut_ids lists ",<variant id>," for those.
  endcomment
  assign cut_ids = ','
  assign pbx = settings.pair_product_b
  if studio_on and pbx != blank
    for pv in pbx.variants
      assign xid = pv.id | append: ''
      assign hits = 0
      for n in (1..10)
        assign kv = 'studio_' | append: n | append: '_variant'
        assign ki = 'studio_' | append: n | append: '_image'
        assign sv = settings[kv] | append: '' | strip
        if sv == xid and settings[ki] != blank
          assign hits = hits | plus: 1
        endif
      endfor
      if hits > 1
        assign cut_ids = cut_ids | append: xid | append: ','
      endif
    endfor
  endif
-%}
<script type="application/json" data-cutout-map>
{"studio":{{ studio_on | json }},"v":{
{%- assign first_v = true -%}
{%- for p in collections.all.products limit: 24 -%}
  {%- for v in p.variants -%}
    {%- liquid
      assign ti = 0
      assign needle = ',' | append: v.id | append: ','
      if cut_ids contains needle
        assign ti = 1
      endif
    -%}
    {%- capture src -%}{% render 'studio-image', variant: v, product: p, index: ti, output: 'url', url_width: 240 %}{%- endcapture -%}
    {%- assign src = src | strip -%}
    {%- capture lbl -%}{%- if p.variants.size > 1 -%}{% render 'zvlabel', t: v.title %}{%- endif -%}{%- endcapture -%}
    {%- unless first_v -%},{%- endunless -%}{%- assign first_v = false -%}
    "{{ v.id }}":{"p":{{ p.id }},"src":{% if src != blank %}{{ src | json }}{% else %}null{% endif %},"label":{{ lbl | strip | json }}}
  {%- endfor -%}
{%- endfor -%}
}}
</script>
